description:
Simplify the Studio revenue gallery composition into a cleaner, quieter analytics card with less nested card treatment and less visual redundancy.

Owner direction:

* Apply these changes only to the Studio revenue composition.
* Preserve its core purpose as a revenue analytics showcase.
* Do not redesign the broader gallery or shared chart system unless a local composition change requires it.

1. Remove title/subtitle header

Remove:

* "Studio revenue"
* "Income against costs, this week." or equivalent subtitle copy

The Week / Month / Quarter tabs should become the first visible content at the top of the card.

Preserve:

* current tab behavior;
* current selected-state treatment;
* keyboard/focus behavior;
* responsive layout.

2. Simplify the three summary metrics

Current summary blocks:

* Revenue
* Margin
* Invoices paid

Remove the individual bordered/card containers around each metric.

Instead:

* present the three metrics in one shared row;
* separate them with vertical line separators;
* keep their labels and primary values;
* keep the small trend badges if they remain visually balanced.

Conceptual structure:

```
Revenue        | Margin        | Invoices paid
$48.2k +12.4%  | 58% +3 pts    | 14 +3
```

Separator requirements:

* short/contained vertical separators between metrics;
* use semantic border tokens;
* no nested mini-card borders/backgrounds;
* responsive collapse should remain coherent.

3. Simplify the chart

Remove:

* the Revenue / Costs legend labels above the chart;
* the secondary Costs dashed/broken line series.

Keep:

* the primary Revenue line/area visualization;
* x-axis/day labels;
* current token-driven chart styling;
* responsive behavior.

The chart should read as one clear primary metric visualization rather than a two-series comparison.

4. Preserve token/system behavior

Keep all styling responsive to Personal UI semantic tokens:

* colors;
* typography roles;
* spacing;
* radius where still relevant;
* borders;
* chart colors;
* light/dark mode.

Do not hard-code raw visual values when semantic tokens are available.

5. Interaction scope

This composition should remain simple and stable:

* tabs may still work;
* no interaction should materially change the card height;
* no additional workflow logic is needed;
* align with the simplification direction from <issue id="1f9debae-21cb-44f0-803a-bd1a38ec55f9" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-84/simplify-gallery-card-interactions-and-preserve-stable-geometry">PUI-84</issue>.

Do not:

* change shared chart primitives unless strictly necessary;
* alter other gallery compositions;
* add new public resources;
* reintroduce nested card surfaces around the metrics;
* add new chart series or legends;
* change gallery ordering/layout in this ticket.

Acceptance:

* Studio revenue no longer shows a title/subtitle header.
* Week / Month / Quarter tabs are the top content.
* Revenue, Margin, and Invoices paid are displayed without individual mini-card containers.
* Vertical separators visually divide the three metrics.
* Trend badges remain only if they fit cleanly.
* Revenue / Costs legend is removed.
* Costs dashed series is removed.
* Primary Revenue chart remains.
* X-axis labels remain.
* Composition height remains stable during interaction.
* Light/dark/theme-token responsiveness remains intact.
* No regression to tabs, focus, responsive containment, or accessibility.
